WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.500
Turkey is a transcontinental nation bridging southeastern Europe and western Asia across the Bosphorus.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Mount Ararat in eastern Turkey rises to 5,137 meters as the highest volcanic peak in the country.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:17.000
In Istanbul, the Hagia Sophia stands with its 31-meter dome as an architectural marvel of Byzantine history.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:23.000
Turkish acoustic music is carried by the long-necked Bağlama lute and the evocative Ney reed flute.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:29.000
Renowned gastronomy features wood-grilled Kebabs, flaky pistachio Baklava, and rich Turkish coffee.

